전문적인 Ruby 소프트웨어 공학을 위한 SOLID 원칙","es":"solid-ruby: Guía de configuración para ingeniería de soft...","fr":"solid-ruby: Guide de mise en place pour l''ingénierie logi...","de":"solid-ruby: Einrichtungsleitfaden für professionelle Soft...","pt":"Guia de Configuração do solid-ruby para Desenvolvedores","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Настройка solid-ruby для Профессионального Раз...","ar":"تدريب عميق على solid-ruby للأدوات الذكية"},"description":{"en":"Unlock expert-level Ruby coding with solid-ruby. Discover how to apply SOLID principles, TDD, and clean code practices for professional software engineering....","zh":"了解 solid-ruby 的技术细节和最佳实践，包括 SOLID 原则、TDD 和设计模式，提高您的 Ruby 编程技能","ja":"solid-ruby の技術的詳細とベストプラクティスを学び、Ruby プログラミングスキルを向上させます","ko":"solid-ruby의 기술적 세부 사항과最佳实践을 배우고 Ruby 프로그래밍 스킬을 향상시키세요","es":"Aprende a dominar solid-ruby, un conjunto de habilidades para ingeniería de software profesional con Ruby y RSpec","fr":"Maîtrisez solid-ruby, un ensemble de compétences pour l''ingénierie logicielle professionnelle avec Ruby et RSpec","de":"Erfahren Sie, wie Sie solid-ruby meistern, ein Satz von Fähigkeiten für professionelle Software-Entwicklung mit Ruby und RSpec","pt":"Aprenda a configurar o solid-ruby com as melhores práticas de engenharia de software e TDD","ru":"Откройте для себя возможности solid-ruby для профессиональной разработки с использованием Ruby и RSpec","ar":"استكشف كيفية دمج solid-ruby في مشاريعك لتحقيق برمجة محترفة"},"definition":{"en":"solid-ruby is a Ruby-oriented skill emphasizing professional software engineering principles, including SOLID, TDD, and clean code, with examples in Ruby and RSpec.","zh":"solid-ruby 是一个 Ruby 软件工程技能，专注于 SOLID 原则、TDD 和设计模式","ja":"solid-ruby は Ruby ソフトウェアエンジニアリングのスキルで、SOLID 原則、TDD 、デザインパターンに焦点を当てています","ko":"solid-ruby는 Ruby 소프트웨어 공학 스킬로 SOLID 원칙, TDD, 디자인 패턴에 중점을 둔 스킬입니다","es":"solid-ruby es un conjunto de habilidades para ingeniería de software profesional que se centra en Ruby y RSpec","fr":"solid-ruby est un ensemble de compétences pour l''ingénierie logicielle professionnelle qui se concentre sur Ruby et RSpec","de":"solid-ruby ist ein Satz von Fähigkeiten für professionelle Software-Entwicklung, der sich auf Ruby und RSpec konzentriert","pt":"O que é solid-ruby? Uma habilidade de engenharia de software que usa Ruby e RSpec","ru":"Что такое solid-ruby? Навык программной инженерии, использующий Ruby и RSpec","ar":"ما هو solid-ruby؟ مهارة في هندسة البرمجيات التي تستخدم Ruby و RSpec"},"features":{"en":["Applies SOLID principles to Ruby development","Utilizes TDD with RSpec for robust testing","Emphasizes clean code practices for maintainable software","Provides examples in Ruby for professional software engineering","Focuses on design patterns for scalable software development","Encourages refactoring for improved code quality"],"zh":["基于 Ruby 的 SOLID 原则","TDD 和测试驱动开发","设计模式和专业软件工程","Ruby 面向对象编程","RSpec 测试框架","专业的代码重构和优化"],"ja":["Ruby ベースの SOLID 原則","TDD とテスト駆動開発","デザインパターンとプロフェッショナルなソフトウェアエンジニアリング","Ruby オブジェクト指向プログラミング","RSpec テストフレームワーク","プロフェッショナルなコードリファクタリングと最適化"],"ko":["Ruby 기반의 SOLID 원칙","TDD와 테스트 주도 개발","디자인 패턴과 전문적인 소프트웨어 공학","Ruby 객체 지향 프로그래밍","RSpec 테스트 프레임워크","전문적인 코드 리팩토링과 최적화"],"es":["Principios SOLID para una mejor estructura de código","Desarrollo dirigido por pruebas (TDD) con RSpec","Diseño de patrones para una arquitectura de software más efectiva","Refactorización de código para mejorar la calidad y la legibilidad","Uso de Ruby como lenguaje de programación principal"],"fr":["Principes SOLID pour une meilleure structure de code","Développement dirigé par les tests (TDD) avec RSpec","Conception de patrons pour une architecture logicielle plus efficace","Refactoring de code pour améliorer la qualité et la lisibilité","Utilisation de Ruby comme langage de programmation principal"],"de":["SOLID-Prinzipien für eine bessere Code-Struktur","Testgetriebene Entwicklung (TDD) mit RSpec","Entwurfsmuster für eine effektivere Software-Architektur","Refaktorisierung von Code für verbesserte Qualität und Lesbarkeit","Verwendung von Ruby als primärer Programmiersprache"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de software com Ruby","Utilização de RSpec para testes","Princípios SOLID para engenharia de software","TDD para desenvolvimento de software","Código limpo e design patterns"],"ru":["Разработка программного обеспечения с помощью Ruby","Использование RSpec для тестирования","Принципы SOLID для программной инженерии","TDD для разработки программного обеспечения","Чистый код и шаблоны проектирования"],"ar":["تطوير البرمجيات باستخدام Ruby","استخدام RSpec للاختبارات","مبادئ SOLID للهندسة البرمجية","TDD لتصميم البرمجيات","كود نظيف وتصميم أنماط"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use solid-ruby","solid-ruby vs ruby on rails","solid-ruby setup guide","what is solid-ruby","solid-ruby alternative to rails","solid-ruby install for professional development","solid-ruby best practices for senior software engineers","solid-ruby and TDD","solid-ruby for clean code"],"zh":["solid-ruby","Ruby 软件工程","SOLID 原则","TDD","设计模式","Ruby 面向对象编程","RSpec","代码重构","AIエージェント"],"ja":["solid-ruby","Ruby ソフトウェアエンジニアリング","SOLID 原則","TDD","デザインパターン","Ruby オブジェクト指向プログラミング","RSpec","コードリファクタリング","AIエージェント"],"ko":["solid-ruby","Ruby 소프트웨어 공학","SOLID 원칙","TDD","디자인 패턴","Ruby 객체 지향 프로그래밍","RSpec","코드 리팩토링","AI 에이전트"],"es":["solid-ruby","ingeniería de software profesional","Ruby","RSpec","principios SOLID","TDD","diseño de patrones","refactorización de código","desarrollo de software con Ruby"],"fr":["solid-ruby","ingénierie logicielle professionnelle","Ruby","RSpec","principes SOLID","TDD","conception de patrons","refactoring de code","développement de logiciels avec Ruby"],"de":["solid-ruby","professionelle Software-Entwicklung","Ruby","RSpec","SOLID-Prinzipien","TDD","Entwurfsmuster","Refaktorisierung von Code","Software-Entwicklung mit Ruby"],"pt":["solid-ruby","desenvolvimento de software","Ruby","RSpec","TDD","SOLID","código limpo","design patterns","engenharia de software"],"ru":["solid-ruby","ИИ Агенты","Разработка программного обеспечения","Ruby","RSpec","TDD","SOLID","Чистый код","Шаблоны проектирования","Программная инженерия"],"ar":["solid-ruby","أدوات ذكية","تطوير البرمجيات","Ruby","RSpec","TDD","SOLID","كود نظيف","تصميم أنماط","هندسة البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"shubhamtaywade82","repo":"trading_playground","repoPath":"shubhamtaywade82/trading_playground","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-08T01:57:15.504Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"solid-ruby","description":"Ruby-focused. Transforms junior-level code into senior-engineer quality software through SOLID, TDD, and clean code. Examples and references use Ruby/RSpec. Use when writing or refactoring Ruby code, planning architecture, reviewing code, or creating tests.","bodyPreview":"# Solid Skills: Professional Software Engineering (Ruby)\n\n**This skill is Ruby-oriented.** All code examples and reference docs use Ruby (and RSpec for tests). The principles (SOLID, TDD, clean code, design patterns) apply to any object-oriented language—these examples are in Ruby.\n\nYou are now operating as a senior software engineer. Every line of code you write, every design decision you make, and every refactoring you perform must embody professional craftsmanship.\n\n## When This Skill Applies","body":"# Solid Skills: Professional Software Engineering (Ruby)\n\n**This skill is Ruby-oriented.** All code examples and reference docs use Ruby (and RSpec for tests). The principles (SOLID, TDD, clean code, design patterns) apply to any object-oriented language—these examples are in Ruby.\n\nYou are now operating as a senior software engineer. Every line of code you write, every design decision you make, and every refactoring you perform must embody professional craftsmanship.\n\n## When This Skill Applies\n\n**ALWAYS use this skill when:**\n- Writing ANY Ruby code (features, fixes, utilities)\n- Refactoring existing Ruby code\n- Planning or designing architecture\n- Reviewing code quality\n- Debugging issues\n- Creating tests (RSpec, Minitest)\n- Making design decisions\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\n> \"Code is to create products for users & customers. Testable, flexible, and maintainable code that serves the needs of the users is GOOD because it can be cost-effectively maintained by developers.\"\n\nThe goal of software: Enable developers to **discover, understand, add, change, remove, test, debug, deploy**, and **monitor** features efficiently.\n\n## The Non-Negotiable Process\n\n### 1. ALWAYS Start with Tests (TDD)\n\n**Red-Green-Refactor is not optional:**\n\n```\n1. RED    - Write a failing test that describes the behavior\n2. GREEN  - Write the SIMPLEST code to make it pass\n3. REFACTOR - Clean up, remove duplication (Rule of Three)\n```\n\n**The Three Laws of TDD:**\n1. You cannot write production code unless it makes a failing test pass\n2. You cannot write more test code than is sufficient to fail\n3. You cannot write more production code than is sufficient to pass\n\n**Design happens during REFACTORING, not during coding.**\n\nSee: [references/tdd.md](references/tdd.md)\n\n### 2. Apply SOLID Principles Rigorously\n\nEvery class, every module, every method:\n\n| Principle                       | Question to Ask                                   |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| **S**RP - Single Responsibility | \"Does this have ONE reason to change?\"            |\n| **O**CP - Open/Closed           | \"Can I extend without modifying?\"                 |\n| **L**SP - Liskov Substitution   | \"Can subtypes replace base types safely?\"         |\n| **I**SP - Interface Segregation | \"Are clients forced to depend on unused methods?\" |\n| **D**IP - Dependency Inversion  | \"Do high-level modules depend on abstractions?\"   |\n\nSee: [references/solid-principles.md](references/solid-principles.md)\n\n### 3. Write Clean, Human-Readable Code\n\n**Naming (in order of priority):**\n1. **Consistency** - Same concept = same name everywhere\n2. **Understandability** - Domain language, not technical jargon\n3. **Specificity** - Precise, not vague (avoid `data`, `info`, `manager`)\n4. **Brevity** - Short but not cryptic\n5. **Searchability** - Unique, greppable names\n\n**Structure:**\n- One level of indentation per method\n- Guard clauses and early returns; avoid `else` when possible\n- **Wrap primitives in value objects** - IDs, emails, money amounts, etc.\n- First-class collections (wrap arrays in dedicated classes)\n- One dot per line (Law of Demeter)\n- Keep classes small (< 50 lines), methods small (< 10 lines)\n- No more than two instance variables per class\n\n**Value Objects in Ruby:**\n```ruby\n# ALWAYS create value objects for domain concepts:\nclass UserId\n  def initialize(value) = @value = value.freeze\n  attr_reader :value\nend\n\nclass Email\n  def initialize(value)\n    raise InvalidEmail unless value.match?(/\\A[^@]+@[^@]+\\z/)\n    @value = value.freeze\n  end\n  attr_reader :value\nend\n\nclass Money\n  def initialize(amount, currency)\n    @amount = amount\n    @currency = currency.freeze\n  end\n  attr_reader :amount, :currency\nend\n\n# NEVER use raw primitives for domain concepts:\n# BAD: def create_order(user_id:, email:)\n# GOOD: def create_order(user_id: UserId, email: Email)\n```\n\nSee: [references/clean-code.md](references/clean-code.md)\n\n### 4. Design with Responsibility in Mind\n\n**Ask these questions for every class:**\n1. \"What pattern is this?\" (Entity, Service, Repository, Factory, etc.)\n2. \"Is it doing too much?\" (Check object calisthenics)\n\n**Object Stereotypes:**\n- **Information Holder** - Holds data, minimal behavior\n- **Structurer** - Manages relationships between objects\n- **Service Provider** - Performs work, stateless operations\n- **Coordinator** - Orchestrates multiple services\n- **Controller** - Makes decisions, delegates work\n- **Interfacer** - Transforms data between systems\n\nSee: [references/object-design.md](references/object-design.md)\n\n### 5. Manage Complexity Ruthlessly\n\n**Essential complexity** = inherent to the problem domain\n**Accidental complexity** = introduced by our solutions\n\n**Fight complexity with:**\n- YAGNI - Don''t build what you don''t need NOW\n- KISS - Simplest solution that works\n- DRY - But only after Rule of Three (wait for 3 duplications)\n\nSee: [references/complexity.md](references/complexity.md)\n\n### 6. Architect for Change\n\n**Vertical Slicing:** Features as end-to-end slices; each feature self-contained.\n\n**Dependency Rule:** Dependencies point toward high-level policies. Infrastructure depends on domain, never reverse. Prefer dependency injection and interfaces (abstract classes or duck-typed contracts).\n\nSee: [references/architecture.md](references/architecture.md)\n\n## The Four Elements of Simple Design (XP)\n\n1. **Runs all the tests** - Must work correctly\n2. **Expresses intent** - Readable, reveals purpose\n3. **No duplication** - DRY (but Rule of Three)\n4. **Minimal** - Fewest classes, methods possible\n\n## Code Smell Detection\n\n**Stop and refactor when you see:** Long Method, Large Class, Long Parameter List, Divergent Change, Shotgun Surgery, Feature Envy, Data Clumps, Primitive Obsession, Switch/type checks (replace with polymorphism), Speculative Generality.\n\nSee: [references/code-smells.md](references/code-smells.md)\n\n## Design Patterns Awareness\n\n**Creational:** Singleton, Factory, Builder\n**Structural:** Adapter, Decorator, Composite\n**Behavioral:** Strategy, Observer, Template Method, Command\n\nDon''t force patterns. Let them emerge from refactoring.\n\nSee: [references/design-patterns.md](references/design-patterns.md)\n\n## Testing Strategy (RSpec)\n\n**Arrange-Act-Assert:**\n```ruby\n# Arrange - Set up test state\ncalculator = Calculator.new\n\n# Act - Execute the behavior\nresult = calculator.add(2, 3)\n\n# Assert - Verify the outcome\nexpect(result).to eq(5)\n```\n\n**Test naming:** Use concrete examples, not abstract statements.\n```ruby\n# BAD: it ''can add numbers''\n# GOOD: it ''returns 5 when adding 2 and 3''\n```\n\nSee: [references/testing.md](references/testing.md)\n\n## Behavioral Principles\n\n- **Tell, Don''t Ask** - Command objects; don''t query and decide\n- **Law of Demeter** - Only talk to immediate friends (one dot per line)\n- **Design by Contract** - Preconditions, postconditions, invariants\n\n## Pre-Code Checklist\n\n1. [ ] Do I understand the requirement? (Write acceptance criteria first)\n2. [ ] What test will I write first?\n3. [ ] What is the simplest solution?\n4. [ ] Am I solving a real problem or a hypothetical one?\n\n## Red Flags - Stop and Rethink\n\n- Writing code without a test\n- Class with more than 2 instance variables\n- Method longer than 10 lines\n- More than one level of indentation\n- Using `else` when early return works\n- Creating abstractions before the third duplication\n- Depending on concrete classes instead of injecting dependencies\n\n## Remember\n\n> \"A little bit of duplication is 10x better than the wrong abstraction.\"\n\n> \"Focus on WHAT needs to happen, not HOW it needs to happen.\"\n\nYour goal: internalize these principles so you write SOLID, testable Ruby by habit.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-08T02:10:21.254Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Generation Agents needing expertise in Ruby-based professional software engineering with SOLID principles and TDD","zh":"非常适合需要在基于Ruby的专业软件工程中掌握SOLID原则和TDD的代码生成代理","ja":"RubyベースのプロフェッショナルなソフトウェアエンジニアリングでSOLID原則とTDDに精通しているコード生成エージェントに最適","ko":"루비 기반 전문 소프트웨어 엔지니어링에서 SOLID 원칙 및 TDD에 精通한 코드 생성 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de generación de código que necesitan experiencia en ingeniería de software profesional basada en Ruby con principios SOLID y TDD","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de génération de code ayant besoin d''expertise en ingénierie de logiciels professionnelle basée sur Ruby avec des principes SOLID et TDD","de":"Perfekt für Code-Generierungsagenten, die Expertenwissen in Ruby-basierter professioneller Softwareentwicklung mit SOLID-Prinzipien und TDD benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Geração de Código que necessitam de especialização em engenharia de software profissional baseada em Ruby com princípios SOLID e TDD","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов генерации кода, которым необходимы знания в области профессиональной разработки программного обеспечения на основе Ruby с принципами SOLID и TDD","ar":"مثالي لعميل توليد الشفرة الذين يحتاجون إلى خبرة في هندسة البرمجيات المهنية القائمة على روبي مع مبادئ SOLID و TDD"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to craft clean, modular Ruby code using SOLID principles, Test-Driven Development, and design patterns, with RSpec for tests, elevating their software engineering capabilities","zh":"赋予代理创建干净、模块化的Ruby代码的能力，使用SOLID原则、测试驱动开发和设计模式，并使用RSpec进行测试，从而提高他们的软件工程能力","ja":"SOLID原則、テスト駆動開発、デザインパターンを使用してクリーンでモジュール化されたRubyコードを作成する能力をエージェントに与え、RSpecを使用してテストを行い、ソフトウェアエンジニアリング能力を向上させる","ko":"SOLID 원칙, 테스트 주도 개발, 디자인 패턴을 사용하여 깨끗하고 모듈화된 루비 코드를 작성하는 능력을 에이전트에게 부여하며, RSpec을 사용하여 테스트를 수행하여 소프트웨어 엔지니어링 능력을 향상시킴","es":"Permite a los agentes crear código Ruby limpio y modular utilizando principios SOLID, Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas y patrones de diseño, con RSpec para pruebas, lo que eleva sus capacidades de ingeniería de software","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer du code Ruby propre et modulaire en utilisant des principes SOLID, un développement piloté par les tests et des modèles de conception, avec RSpec pour les tests, ce qui améliore leurs capacités d''ingénierie logicielle","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, sauberen, modularen Ruby-Code mit SOLID-Prinzipien, testgetriebenem Entwickeln und Entwurfsmustern zu erstellen, mit RSpec für Tests, und hebt damit ihre Software-Entwicklungs-Fähigkeiten","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar código Ruby limpo e modular usando princípios SOLID, Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes e padrões de design, com RSpec para testes, elevando suas capacidades de engenharia de software","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать чистый и модульный код Ruby с использованием принципов SOLID, Test-Driven Development и шаблонов проектирования, а также RSpec для тестов, повышая их возможности в области разработки программного обеспечения","ar":"يمنح العميل القدرة على صياغة رمز روبي نظيف ومتجاوب باستخدام مبادئ SOLID والتحكم في التطوير والتصاميم النمطية، مع RSpec للاختبارات، مما يرفع من قدراتهم في مجال هندسة البرمجيات"},"useCases":{"en":["Refactoring legacy Ruby codebases for improved maintainability","Implementing design patterns in Ruby for scalable software design","Writing unit tests with RSpec for robust test coverage"],"zh":["为改善可维护性而重构遗留的Ruby代码库","在Ruby中实现设计模式以实现可扩展的软件设计","使用RSpec编写单元测试以实现强大的测试覆盖"],"ja":["保守性を向上させるためにレガシーのRubyコードベースをリファクタリングする","Rubyでデザインパターンを実装してスケーラブルなソフトウェアデザインを実現する","RSpecを使用して単体テストを記述して強力なテストカバレッジを実現する"],"ko":["유지 보수성을 개선하기 위해 레거시 루비 코드베이스를 리팩터링하는 것","루비에서 디자인 패턴을 구현하여 확장 가능한 소프트웨어 디자인을 구현하는 것","RSpec을 사용하여 단위 테스트를 작성하여 강력한 테스트 커버리지를 구현하는 것"],"es":["Reestructuración de código legacy Ruby para mejorar la mantenibilidad","Implementación de patrones de diseño en Ruby para un diseño de software escalable","Escritura de pruebas unitarias con RSpec para una cobertura de pruebas robusta"],"fr":["Réorganisation de code legacy Ruby pour améliorer la maintenabilité","Mise en œuvre de modèles de conception en Ruby pour un design de logiciel évolutif","Réduction d''unités de test avec RSpec pour une couverture de test robuste"],"de":["Refaktorisierung von Legacy-Ruby-Code für verbesserte Wartbarkeit","Implementierung von Entwurfsmustern in Ruby für skalierbaren Software-Design","Schreiben von Einheitstests mit RSpec für robuste Testabdeckung"],"pt":["Reestruturação de bases de código Ruby legadas para melhor manutenibilidade","Implementação de padrões de design em Ruby para design de software escalável","Escrita de testes unitários com RSpec para cobertura de teste robusta"],"ru":["Рефакторинг устаревших баз кода Ruby для улучшения поддерживаемости","Реализация шаблонов проектирования в Ruby для масштабируемого дизайна программного обеспечения","Написание модульных тестов с помощью RSpec для надёжного покрытия тестами"],"ar":["إعادة هيكلة قواعد بيانات روبي قديمة لتحسين الصيانة","تنفيذ أنماط التصميم في روبي لتصميم البرمجيات القابل للتوسعة","كتابة الاختبارات الوحدوية مع RSpec لتغطية الاختبار القوية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Ruby-oriented, may require additional adaptation for other programming languages","Requires understanding of object-oriented programming concepts"],"zh":["面向Ruby，可能需要为其他编程语言进行额外的适配","需要理解面向对象编程概念"],"ja":["Ruby向けであるため、他のプログラミング言語には追加の適応が必要になる可能性がある","オブジェクト指向プログラミングの概念を理解する必要がある"],"ko":["루비 지향이므로 다른 프로그래밍 언어에는 추가적인 적응이 필요할 수 있음","객체 지향 프로그래밍 개념을 이해해야 함"],"es":["Orientado a Ruby, puede requerir adaptación adicional para otros lenguajes de programación","Requiere comprensión de conceptos de programación orientada a objetos"],"fr":["Orienté Ruby, peut nécessiter une adaptation supplémentaire pour d''autres langages de programmation","Nécessite une compréhension des concepts de programmation orientée objet"],"de":["Ruby-orientiert, kann zusätzliche Anpassung für andere Programmiersprachen erfordern","Benötigt Verständnis von objektorientierten Programmierkonzepten"],"pt":["Orientado para Ruby, pode exigir adaptação adicional para outras linguagens de programação","Exige compreensão de conceitos de programação orientada a objetos"],"ru":["Ориентирован на Ruby, может потребовать дополнительной адаптации для других языков программирования","Требует понимания концепций объектно-ориентированного программирования"],"ar":["موجهة نحو روبي، قد تتطلب التكيف الإضافي للغات البرمجة الأخرى","يتطلب فهم مفاهيم البرمجة الموجهة للكائنات"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"eabff7c702f5648b72d6f4d4eab8135673fed492077839b8b935a79625c2f8b4","qualityScore":36}');
